1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:15,292
ZADP puts seller-signed offers into Zcash shielded memos. Independent indexers turn those
publications into searchable discovery data. The discovery host can change while the
signed offers remain on chain.

2
00:00:15,942 --> 00:00:30,583
A seller signs an Offer and publishes it to a board through a Zcash transaction. The
signature binds the declared terms to that board. A signature authenticates the
declaration; it does not guarantee service quality.

3
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:46,667
An indexer uses chain data and a signed board descriptor, including its dedicated incoming
viewing key. It verifies offers and board admission, then builds a local index. Scanning
requires no wallet spending keys.

4
00:00:47,317 --> 00:01:01,917
Humans and agents can search the same discovery data. A browser uses the API; an agent can
use the read-only MCP adapter. Geographic matching can keep the buyer location in browser
memory.

5
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:19,542
A discovery-only announcement needs no service endpoint or price. For supported commerce,
orders and results go directly to the seller. A separate buyer wallet approves payment.
The discovery indexer does not hold spending authority.

6
00:01:20,192 --> 00:01:36,167
The proposed sharing layer would distribute a signed descriptor and a dedicated board
incoming viewing key. A recipient could independently reconstruct the same board. This
grants incoming visibility, never permission to spend its funds.

7
00:01:36,817 --> 00:01:53,042
An operator could pin the trusted descriptor and rescan from its birthday. If one
discovery host disappears, another could restore visibility without sellers republishing.
Local moderation may still produce different visible results.

8
00:01:53,692 --> 00:02:12,583
An indexer could serve several independently shared boards. Each keeps its own signed
admission policy and isolated state. Hosts may apply local visibility rules for different
jurisdictions. Sharing does not move an Offer into another board or establish legality.

9
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:32,125
Use a dedicated board viewing key, never personal wallet keys. Pin descriptor trust
independently. Shared incoming data cannot be made secret again. Reconstruction already
exists; opt-in sharing, distribution and lifecycle design remain future work.
